WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.170
I brought you some water, Ms. Sarasa.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.330
Thanks, Lorea...

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.960
A-are you alright?!

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.040
I really pushed the physical enhancement,
so my whole body is aching.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.170
Normal potions won't do
anything about it, either...

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.880
Is that so...?

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.500
Sorry, Lorea...

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.040
Please, don't worry about it.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.580
After all, it's thanks to you
that we were able to save the village!

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.710
No, it's because everyone worked together.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:34.830
Ms. Owner!

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.670
Ms. Iris? Ms. Kate?

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:41.130
Please, take nourishment from these, Ms. Owner.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.420
Ah, thank you!

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:44.960
You gathered so many!

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.580
Well, we do have a debt to repay
and everything...

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.540
As you can see, I have fully recovered!

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.460
If there is anything I can do to help,
please don't hesitate to ask.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.670
In that case, could you go ahead and live here?

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:04.670
A-ah, my deepest apologies, but we could
not possibly pay rent on top of our debt...

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.250
That wouldn't be necessary.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.670
And if you can avoid lodging fees,

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:10.290
it should make the burden of repaying me
weigh less on you, right?

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.710
Well, yeah...

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.710
It would be a big help for me too,
as I need alchemic ingredients,

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:21.460
and it would be useful to have access to
the sort of information gatherers hear.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.330
Please, lend me a hand
with running my business!

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:37.790
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.210
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:44.500
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.750
Udemakutte arukidasou

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.960
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.210
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:59.580
Jiyuu sugiru tte nante fujiyuu nan deshou

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.920
Datte tokenai no yo

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.330
Rironchi jikkenchi spiral

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.420
Maido utedo katte mo

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.000
(Nani o tameshite mite mo)

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.670
Nengan kanatte shikuhakku

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.500
(Cheat ja nai yo life hack)

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.960
Harete ippo fumidaseru license

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.210
Kore kara ga hajimari

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.460
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.880
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.250
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.830
Shigoto no mae wa shinkokyuu

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:37.000
Hibike te o nobashita shintenchi

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.330
Yume wa kitto te no naka

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.750
Kitto dekiru original

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.460
Door o akete welcome de ikou

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.960
(Sore ja koko ga start)

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.460
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.880
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.080
I don't even know what to say...

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.130
Well, the view is better now.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.500
How is everywhere else looking?

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.460
From what I confirmed, there were
a number of houses with broken walls,

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.000
one that was half destroyed,

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.170
and another that was burned down.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.790
That's some serious damage.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:23.710
The one silver lining is that they were all
vacant houses meant for loaning out to gatherers.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:29.080
Then does that mean the most serious
damage here was to your shop, Ms. Sarasa?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.670
It's true that you couldn't
open the shop like this...

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.250
Ms. Sarasa?

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:38.710
Huh?!

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:40.170
It couldn't be...!

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.750
We're going to open up,
even with things like this?!

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.630
It's precisely because of the state of things.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:51.040
We ended up with that whole mess
right after finally opening.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.630
But a time like this is precisely when

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:57.130
an alchemy shop like mine
can help out the village.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:01.080
I want to help so that everyone
from the village can get back to

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.580
their everyday lives as soon as possible,
and I'm sure I'm capable of it!

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.210
Got it!

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:09.040
We shall lend a hand as well!

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.500
Thank you!

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.920
Alright, we'll start by checking on the village
and letting them know the shop is open.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:15.790
Right!

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.210
Take care!

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.540
Now then...

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:24.630
Alright!

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.630
What is that?

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.330
I guess you'd call it a bit of
preferential treatment towards

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.540
the locals and the gatherers
based in the area.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:37.290
"Discounts available for customers
who bring along used bottles"...?

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.830
Potion containers come in all sorts of
varieties and vary from shop to shop,

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:43.880
so you can't reuse empty ones generally.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:44.750
However...

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.210
When it comes to bottles made here in this shop...

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.080
You can just wash and reuse them!

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:50.830
Yeah!

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:55.630
Most of the effort behind basic potions
comes from just making the bottles!

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.460
And so, if I can buy back the bottles...

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:02.000
It works out for everyone, right?!

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.710
Well, it'll lead to a drop in profits, but still...

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:08.670
But if you make up for that
with your other goods, like...

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:09.460
Ah!

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:11.880
What about this cloth for bedding?

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.540
Ah!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.830
I-it's that expensive...?!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.920
That's 20-30% cheaper
than in the capital, though.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.830
And if I slip up in the process,
it instantly becomes worthless.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:27.330
So, say I were to buy a million rhea
worth of alchemic ingredients,

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.960
if I made a mistake in the process...

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:35.880
That's why alchemists need
a certain level of savings,

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.790
to keep ourselves out of debt.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.580
How harsh...

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:45.130
And so, I've got to think up a way
to earn a bit more profits.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:50.290
Are you feeling all better now, Sarasa?

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.250
Yes, thankfully.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.000
Glad to hear it.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.130
So, what brings you here today?

00:05:56.130 --> 00:06:01.630
I came to negotiate into how the
hell flame grizzly parts are being handled.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.000
Oh?

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.420
I already collected the alchemic ingredients,

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:10.380
but once I receive money for them, I would like
to split that with everyone from the village.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.500
And with Andre's group, who stayed behind
despite knowing the danger.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.920
My proposal is that I'll take forty percent,
and the remainder...

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.080
That won't be necessary.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:20.880
Huh?!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.580
Do as you please with
the ingredients you gathered.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.920
Eh?! Oh no, I couldn't!

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:31.130
You took down over half of
those grizzlies, didn't you?

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:32.170
But...

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:34.580
Nobody will complain about that.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.960
In exchange...

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:42.040
We're currently in the process of
dissecting what was left over.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.330
Would you mind if we took that?

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:46.960
Of course not.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.130
Meat and pelts fundamentally
aren't useful in alchemy.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:52.670
I appreciate it.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:55.460
If we sell that off, it should let us
pay the gatherers who helped out,

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.880
and also cover repairs to the village.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:03.000
But won't it be pretty tough
to sell all of that?

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.460
That's true...

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:10.330
We leave dealings outside of the village
up to Darna from the general store.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.540
He's Lorea's father, isn't he?

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:17.710
We can pickle the meat in salt,
but how will we handle the pelts...?

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:21.380
In that case, why don't I
take charge of the pelts too?

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:22.750
You don't mind?

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.420
Not at all, since I can process them.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.130
Please, leave it to me!

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.920
So, there are 28 bears' worth here...

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.880
Once I transfer the contents of the flame sacs,
that should decrease the volume a good bit.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.630
Are you going to use all of this, Ms. Sarasa?

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:43.540
Ah, no, I couldn't possibly
go through all of it on my own.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.040
And you took charge of the pelts too, right?

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.000
Yeah.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.580
It would be easiest to have
my master buy them, but...

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.040
I guess I'll use the opportunity
to go sell them!

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.790
Huh?! You're going to sell them?!

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:59.250
If I go introduce myself to the
alchemists in the nearest town,

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.210
I'll be able to buy and sell necessary
ingredients with them in the future.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.040
It should make things much more convenient!

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.250
I see.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.380
Hup!

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:11.000
The nearest town to here
would be South Straug, right?

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.330
Well then, I'm counting on you
to man the shop!

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:18.540
Ah, but Ms. Sarasa, it would take three days
to make it to South Straug on foot!

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:21.080
And there aren't any regular carriages
out to there either.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.380
No worries.

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:24.210
I'll be using physical enhancement.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:29.080
I'll be back by tomorrow morning at the latest!

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:42.500
That may have been a bit much, considering
I was bedridden up until yesterday...

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.500
It took me half a day...

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.630
It's a town!

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.830
A normal, proper town!

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.750
There's a clothing store! And a hat shop!

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.790
A bakery and a cake shop!

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.210
There's even a trendy cafe!

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:00.960
It sure would be nice to be able
to take it easy

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.250
and drink tea in a place
like that someday...

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:06.670
I've got to earn money for that too!

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.170
Ah, excuse me!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.330
I'm looking for an alchemist's shop.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:13.380
Oh, we've got two of those.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:16.290
One's right down that alley,

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:19.460
while the other's on the edge of
the town's central plaza.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.040
Thank you!

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:24.040
Alright, I guess I'll start with the closer one.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.080
Hello.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:30.960
Welcome.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.040
Um, I came to sell ingredients.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.960
Hmm? What've you got?

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.830
It's this.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:47.170
Even at a low evaluation, it should
come out to around 300,000 rhea...

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.960
Anger bear hearts, eh?

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.250
Huh?!

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:52.040
Those aren't from anger bears, they're...

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.670
They're a bit old and
weren't handled well either.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.170
I suppose I could offer you
around 12,000 rhea.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:03.540
I'm not some novice who
can't even tell the difference

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.630
between an anger bear
and a hellflame grizzly...

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:09.580
And even if they were anger bears,
to offer only 12,000...!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.420
Plus, he said they were old
and poorly handled.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.500
Is he looking down on me?!

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.290
Well then, what about these?

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:20.710
If you add those in,
I guess I could do 20,000 in total.

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:21.630
That's fine, right?

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:22.630
Excuse me!

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:23.880
Hey, hold on!

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:33.460
Was it a mistake coming here to South Straug?

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.540
If they're going to beat down
prices that much,

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:39.080
I'll have to come up with
a different method...

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:45.580
Still... I already came all this way.

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.500
I'll go give the other shop a try.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:55.960
Alright...!

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.080
Welcome.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.170
Hello.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.040
What brings you here today?

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:17.960
U-um, I wanted to sell these...

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.880
Ooh! This is a hellflame grizzly heart, isn't it?!

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:28.040
It's fresh and handled well,
so 400,000 rhea sounds about right!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.080
Now that I think of it,

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.540
I heard from a gatherer that came in

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:39.290
that he fled from hellflame grizzlies
rampaging towards Yok Village.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:43.540
From what I was told, I figured the village
would have been wiped off the map by now.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.960
But if you have this...

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:48.710
We somehow managed to handle them.

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:52.540
Then are you perhaps the alchemist
who just came to the village?!

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:53.580
Yes!

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:55.960
Huh?

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:58.210
You're Ophelia Millis's apprentice?

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:00.040
That master class alchemist?

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.460
A-ah, yes.

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:04.880
Wow! To think that the apprentice of someone
like that would come all the way out here.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.040
No wonder you're so skilled.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:10.960
Do you mind if I purchase
all the ingredients you brought in today?

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:11.960
Of course not.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:15.460
And there are actually a number of
ingredients I'd like to buy myself.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:19.210
Yes, we've got all of that.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.380
We should be able to work out
a reasonable rate.

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.540
That's a big help!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:25.130
You're the one helping me out!

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:27.630
It's been a big problem how we
haven't had a good flow of ingredients

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:30.250
ever since that old-timer from
Yok Village closed up shop.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:34.210
I'm glad that a skilled alchemist
like you moved there.

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.080
It makes me happy to hear that.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:40.750
If you're ever in trouble,
feel free to consult with me.

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.130
Thank you!

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:45.250
I'm Leonora. And you are?

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:48.000
Ah, I'm Sarasa. Sarasa Feed.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.630
Why don't you stay the night, Sarasa?

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:52.250
Huh?! Ah, no...

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.330
I can't go imposing that much on you...

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.040
If you used physical enhancement to
come here, you must be exhausted, right?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.250
Don't worry about it. You can just
head out early tomorrow morning.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:05.250
Listen to what your senior in alchemy
has to say, alright?

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.380
Right!

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:26.380
I made it!

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:31.130
I'm not quite as tired out since I got
some proper rest last night!

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:36.130
With all those sales, I should be
able to afford repairs on the shop.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:38.130
And it gives me some funds
to work with for the time being.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:42.750
I really am glad to have met
a great alchemist like Ms. Leonora!

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.880
And she even sent me home
with some sweets too!

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:51.880
Is everyone still asleep...?

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:55.710
Ah, welcome back, Ms. Owner!

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:58.330
You're training this early
in the morning, Ms. Iris?

00:13:58.330 --> 00:13:59.330
Indeed.

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:03.920
I wish to be ready at any moment for
whatever unexpected issues may arise.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:05.830
Welcome home.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:08.540
We've handled the repairs
we could do on our own.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.330
Wow, that's a big help!

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:14.380
And I also have a suggestion, Ms. Sarasa!

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:15.500
A suggestion?

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:18.790
Why don't we make a kitchen?!

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:24.500
This is technically the kitchen,
even if it looks like this now...

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:28.170
No, I'm talking about a proper kitchen
where you can cook.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:29.420
A proper one?

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.000
You don't have a stove or oven
or anything, right?

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.920
So why not use the opportunity
to make a full-fledged kitchen?!

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:40.000
I don't really cook much, though...

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.290
I'll do it!

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:42.250
Huh?!

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:47.670
Ms. Iris and Ms. Kate are living here too now,
so let's all eat together!

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:50.670
I'm sure the two of them
would prefer that too!

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:56.630
It's true that it would be cheaper than
eating out if you could prepare something.

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:59.880
And gatherer's make a living
through physical labor, too...

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.000
I guess let's give your proposal a try!

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.290
I'm in agreement too.

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:11.380
Mr. Geberk!

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:15.920
You played the biggest role,
so my pride as the village carpenter

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:19.040
won't accept your house
being left all busted up.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.000
You little ladies must feel
ill at ease too, right?

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.630
Sorry for making you come out here.

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:25.500
I'll give your furniture an upgrade too.

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:27.290
Thank you.

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:30.040
I'll make sure to pay you
properly for your work.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:34.830
Thank you!

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:38.580
Can you handle it?
Be careful on your way back.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.710
Right!

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:43.580
One, two, one, two, one, two...!

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.500
My, what's that iron plate for?

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:50.080
Ah, Mrs. Delal!

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:53.670
It's for the magic stove for our kitchen.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:57.540
Ooh, a magic stove? I sure am jealous.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.670
You don't need any fuel, and you can control
the strength of the flame freely, right?

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:01.540
That's right!

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.880
It's easier, since you don't
need to use flames.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:06.920
I'd love to have one put in too,
but they're expensive...

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:10.830
That's true! It costs 120,000 rhea, after all!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.670
Oh? 120,000?

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:15.710
I heard they went for around
two to three hundred thousand, though.

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:19.250
Ah, I'd imagine that's thanks to
the shipping charges.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:22.040
And it makes a difference if it's
for home or business use too.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.670
For your place, I'd imagine
it's be around 150,000.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.790
150,000, eh? Hmm...

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:31.630
Oh no, I went into business mode there
and launched into my sales talk!

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:32.880
Hmm...

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.040
Please, don't push yourself!

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.920
That sure looks complicated.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:41.380
Not at all.

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:45.420
It's just...

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:48.670
It's a bit of fine work, so it
wears on the nerves, I suppose.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:50.210
Wow...!

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:58.250
I've got to place the magical crystal
in this slot, and then...

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:03.170
We affix the metal plates on top...

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:07.290
Now we just need to use resin to fill the gaps

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:10.330
and add a coating to increase
durability and water resistance,

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:11.460
and we'll be all done.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.130
I'm looking forward to it!

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.130
Coming!

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:17.920
Mrs. Delal?

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.540
Can I have a moment?

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.960
I hesitated over it, but I'll go ahead
and buy some magic stoves.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.170
Two of them!

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:26.080
Huh?! Two?!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.130
Yeah.

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:31.420
Our place uses a crazy amount
of firewood as it is.

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.670
It's a small price to pay,

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:38.000
considering we won't need to secure
and store all that, or even chop it.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.210
Got it!

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:41.830
If you're ordering two at once I can
give you a ten percent discount

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.420
and make it 270,000 rhea!

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:44.920
I appreciate it!

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:47.000
I'll get them made right away!

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:49.830
Hup...!

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.500
That takes care of the delivery!

00:17:57.790 --> 00:17:59.670
My, how wonderful!

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.500
Yeah, this is great!

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.710
Here's your payment.

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:06.250
Ah, I don't mind if you pay in installments.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:07.630
It's fine.

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:10.920
After all, the mayor split the funds from
the whole hellflame grizzly incident

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.330
with all us villagers.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:15.750
And you were the original
source of that, right, Sarasa?

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:17.540
So seriously, thanks.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:22.130
Ah!

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.250
Sarasa!

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.170
Huh?!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.920
Thank you!

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.830
We all made it through safely
because of you!

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.290
Oh, Dad!

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.250
I'm Lorea's father Darna.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.790
Thank you for saving my daughter's life.

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:37.960
I purchased some potions,

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:39.960
and that bottle buyback
you've got going is great!

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:42.210
You alchemists sure are something else!

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:44.630
Please, take this.

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:48.880
Everyone certainly is grateful.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:54.830
You collapsed, and then you were so busy
up until now, Ms. Sarasa.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:59.380
So, everyone's happy to have a chance
to let you know how they feel!

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:05.920
Am I... being accepted after all...?

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.460
It's a kitchen!

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.210
And new furniture,

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:16.750
and the walls too!

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:18.750
Just what I'd expect from Mr. Geberk!

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:19.830
Amazing...!

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:23.790
And the interior looks great thanks to
the coordinating you did, Ms. Kate!

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:25.920
That's for sure!

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:30.250
It looks just as great as I imagined!
No, even better!

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.960
Lorea, I've got a present for you.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:34.580
Here.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:37.170
Ah, is that a cookbook?!

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:41.540
You see, I had my master send it over
with the transfer circle.

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:44.420
So technically, it's a present from her!

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.250
Thank you!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:49.130
I'll be sure to make lots of delicious meals!

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:51.670
I'm looking forward to it.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:52.670
Yeah!

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.000
Now then...

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:57.500
Why don't we try boiling water to make sure
the stove's working alright?

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:00.080
How about we go ahead
and put on some tea?

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.210
That sounds great!

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:06.210
In that case, we should help ourselves
to the sweets from Ms. Leonora too!

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.210
Delicious!

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.750
It's been a while since I've had any sweets.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:20.290
It has a sort of city taste to it, somehow!

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:21.960
Please, have more.

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:24.710
Sweets just go great with tea, don't they?

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:26.250
You've got that right!

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:29.080
Ooh, this one tastes different!

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:30.290
Which one?

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:31.580
You're right!

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:36.830
Hmm? I feel like we're forgetting
something important...

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:41.920
Allow me to borrow the bath, Ms...

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:42.750
Huh?!

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:49.080
Ah, we completely forgot to let Ms. Iris know!

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:52.920
I'm so sorry! Things just sort of
flowed into having a tea party!

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:54.920
I want to eat sweets too!

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.380
Don't worry, there are still some left.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:00.040
You can't fool me, Kate!

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:00.830
Eh?!

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:04.500
What is it that you're hiding there?!

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:07.630
Ah, I was saving those to give to you later...

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:10.330
Then I'll do this!

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:13.880
So good! Delicious!

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.960
See, that's because you shoveled it all in.

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:21.000
Come on, have some tea!

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.330
M-my apologies!

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:27.000
Now you've gone and drank too much!

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:38.330
Let's have that apple
you were given before too.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:40.080
Agreed!

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:47.210
I've got to think on how to run my shop

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:51.540
so that we and everyone from the village can
spend every day with smiles on our faces.

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:55.920
It's not just about the big
and small things I can make.

00:21:56.670 --> 00:22:01.830
I'd like to come up with product
people can use in their everyday lives...

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:04.130
So tasty!

00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:31.210
Mado kara fuwari sashikomu hizashi

00:22:31.500 --> 00:22:37.000
Mezame no yokan ga sasayakikakeru

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:43.040
Kitai to sukoshi no yuuki tsurete

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:48.580
Seichou no kakera sageshi ni ikou

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:54.920
Hajimete hiraku tobira sotto nozokeba

00:22:54.920 --> 00:23:02.460
Dokidoki ga tsunaideku takusan no egao

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:10.040
